ll:fd7cc56b96a149a192520a5d90418d62 a ll:Diagnosis ;
    ll:because ll:887624952fa64d96b69887c4319e2c00 ;
    ll:created "2026-11-11T04:07:57.825265+00:00" ;
    ll:experiment ll:9ab34a66f69742b2aaf35aca345f4861 ;
    ll:text "The maternal left endpoint is unphased at GQ 9, and the VCF implies maternal HP2 at both flanking markers. The three eligible maternal-origin child reads spanning both endpoints and both flanks carry C/C/A/A, a pattern also present in four maternal HP1-tagged reads and one paternal read. Three other maternal HP1-tagged reads carry T at the left endpoint, so that tag contains both C and T there. The phase-grouped IGV view shows alignments spanning the flanks in the child and both parents. The audited bases leave the maternal switch unresolved. Resolving the maternal phase at the left endpoint and linking it to additional informative markers on child reads would help." .

ll:heuristic_5fce197902b9a8e508612549 a ll:Heuristic ;
    ll:because ll:2a0a613144da4095a574ae857b63b555,
        ll:73f27d21641d41678a65661478c56b80,
        ll:81659e3fa5f34c719e2e5984382fb6a6 ;
    ll:created "2026-11-11T04:14:24.327884+00:00" ;
    ll:experiment ll:6e5dde445b484d4e91f5fbbb4b623b71 ;
    ll:status "proposed" ;
    ll:test "Reuse child_origins, phase_support, phase_supported, and spanning from trio_flank_linkage.py. Add a branch for candidates that fail endpoint eligibility, and evaluate read linkage directly between qualifying flanks without requiring the endpoint alleles. Prespecify the search radius, minimum molecule count, and parental coverage criteria. On held-out trio candidates with independently adjudicated switches and artifacts, compare the existing audit with and without this branch at a fixed false-positive rate. Measure how many additional confirmed switches it recovers and how wide their reported intervals are. Keep both maternal review cases as unresolved regression checks." ;
    ll:text "Test whether confidently phased flanking markers can rescue crossover candidates with a low-quality, unphased, or read-discordant endpoint. The current audit requires both endpoints to pass before counting switch-supporting reads. A rescue call would require multiple child molecules to link opposite parental haplotypes at flanking markers in the same parental phase set, with parental reads corroborating marker phase and a Mendelian anchor corroborating child origin on at least one of those molecules. Report the interval between the corroborating markers. In the supported paternal case, three child reads linked upstream HP1 and downstream HP2 markers. One unresolved maternal case had only a downstream HP1 link on a read without a direct origin anchor. The other had no qualifying flanks, and all eight maternal HP2-tagged reads at the right endpoint disagreed with the VCF phase. Both maternal cases would remain unresolved under this rule. Whether the rule recovers additional genuine switches remains untested." .

ll:heuristic_8d6779429db1e79ea69cd632 a ll:Heuristic ;
    ll:because ll:07e889d3f722427c81c21fe482365c69,
        ll:324f470874c44773af835ea84c8a74a7,
        ll:887624952fa64d96b69887c4319e2c00 ;
    ll:created "2026-11-11T04:08:27.874827+00:00" ;
    ll:experiment ll:9ab34a66f69742b2aaf35aca345f4861 ;
    ll:status "proposed" ;
    ll:test "Reuse collect_markers and read_observations from trio_baseline.py and spanning_counts from critic_trio_audit.py. Replace the audit's hand-selected marker panels with an automatic search using a prespecified window and marker-quality criteria. Compare endpoint-only and augmented rankings on held-out trio candidates with independently adjudicated switches and artifacts. At a fixed review budget, test whether the augmented ranking recovers more confirmed switches, and report how often insufficient informative read coverage leaves candidates unresolved. Use the three reviewed loci as regression cases and keep the two maternal cases labeled unresolved." ;
    ll:text "Test whether ranking crossover candidates by read-linked support from additional informative markers improves on ranking by endpoint evidence alone. For each candidate, look on both sides for confidently phased markers in the same phase set of the transmitting parent. Up-rank a switch when child reads assigned to that parent link the candidate to markers that corroborate the inferred haplotype on each side and the parental reads support the marker phase. In the supported paternal case, child reads linked the endpoint pattern to an upstream paternal-origin anchor, and two child reads linked that same endpoint pattern to two downstream HP2 markers beyond the original window. In both unresolved maternal cases, the longer child patterns also occurred in parental reads, and a low-quality or unphased endpoint weakened the haplotype assignment. Sparse coverage or a lack of informative markers can leave a genuine switch unresolved, so retain such candidates for review. These three reviews motivate the hypothesis but do not establish a gain in detection accuracy." .

