ll:ce57c12dfc4e418c8c3af8bddea4e9d5 a ll:CrossoverCandidate ;
    ll:created "2026-11-11T04:04:03.069107+00:00" ;
    ll:experiment ll:9ab34a66f69742b2aaf35aca345f4861 ;
    ll:files ll:1ffadb014fe84e4ba5d5afb06114acd0,
        ll:3e39800c27ce42a280729243641d692b,
        ll:7049c238332a4318be56870345d62d12,
        ll:81e936eaabeb4bd493090ca4704a876f,
        ll:cbd408e29298418caad6c4af1e7682b4,
        ll:e7643c3f724347dca263619c6d9a21f0,
        ll:e7a30e558acd4898bd7c47546a5ef38a,
        ll:fd83b38046ef40da8044c160fdbdfe73 ;
    ll:status "proposed" ;
    ll:text "The trio genotypes imply paternal HP1 at 20,959,352 and HP2 at 20,961,970 within paternal phase set 19256651. A Mendelian marker at 20,955,483 anchors child HP1 to the father. Eight child HP1 reads carry G/G across the endpoints, and six of those also carry the paternal G allele at the upstream anchor. The father has 17 G/A and 17 A/G spanning reads, with zero G/G, while the mother has 26 G/A and 23 A/G, with zero G/G. These observations support a paternal crossover between the listed markers. The right endpoint is the only resolved paternal HP2 marker in the analyzed window." .

ll:ce9b2f4bca5b48ccb52fa75bd020f545 a ll:CrossoverCandidate ;
    ll:created "2026-11-11T04:12:23.210511+00:00" ;
    ll:experiment ll:6e5dde445b484d4e91f5fbbb4b623b71 ;
    ll:files ll:0c62106340b8404b8246587783dfe4d8,
        ll:3349f17cb64b4c04be72109201b84bb2,
        ll:530d0a880c8b495eaccec7ae1a801960,
        ll:538ac7a8b3244b93840a620c3805fdcc,
        ll:54c54e2fcb1b456cbd0f6699bb72d904,
        ll:58a72f4e7f52473d824f7ee96c48bd0d,
        ll:5ea7c1e672d6423b9858840110a4b2f8,
        ll:66f254951c1242d6bfc4b6db374dc107,
        ll:a7111596beef47898326e41d4d5e2af0,
        ll:bf24ba822e52407f8016f1fb125e47df,
        ll:cfd8440182bf44f08b55286940a9e431,
        ll:d5ccbb91f2d14bf5be1c9f7c0b5dfcf8,
        ll:e91afd62dcff436dbc34b21a12b39d3a ;
    ll:status "proposed" ;
    ll:text "The maternal switch remains unresolved. The left endpoint is unphased at maternal GQ 9. At the right endpoint, the VCF assigns A to maternal HP2, while all eight eligible HP2-tagged maternal reads covering that base carry G. The baseline assigns three C/A child reads to maternal origin, and the same endpoint pair occurs in four maternal reads and one paternal read. Under the stricter follow-up criteria, no flanking marker qualified on either side and no endpoint-spanning child read could be assigned maternal origin." .

