        ll:ede008ad834c48e28c08b7cd8f7429fb ;
    ll:status "proposed" ;
    ll:text "The maternal left endpoint is unphased in the VCF at GQ 9. Three child reads on the maternally assigned child HP1 carry C/A across the endpoints, a pair also observed in four maternal reads and one paternal read. Those same three child reads carry C/C/A/A at 21,290,886, 21,291,740, 21,291,798 and 21,292,406, matching four maternal HP1 reads and one paternal read across all four sites. The phased VCF assigns maternal HP2 at both flanking markers. The existing maternal read pattern and sparse eligible child coverage leave the proposed switch unresolved." .

